The v1 shipped band answers {{v:v1_cov}} of windows at {{v:v1_acc_band}} accuracy and alerts {{v:v1_alert_band}} of all hypoxic windows; the v2 chain with its pulse-lock gate answers {{v:v2_cov}} at {{v:v2_acc_band}} and alerts {{v:v2_alert_band}}. Abstention is not detection: unanswered hypoxic windows are missed.

### 8.3 Calibration and conformal 3-state output

The nested conformal result below supersedes the descriptive ranking above where the two differ: it fixes the cutoffs from other people only.

{{@conformal_full}}

![Conformal output](docs/figures/ml_conformal.png)

**Reading.** The numbers for the model the app runs are the **deployed pipeline R** rows. They are exploratory and optimistic (R was chosen with all six people in view); the per-person-selected rows are the nested estimate of the selection procedure. The deployed pipeline does not beat v1 at matched coverage ({{cm:deployed_R/v1/conformal_mondrian|d}} points at v1's coverage, {{cm:deployed_R/v2/conformal_mondrian|d}} at v2's; both intervals contain zero), and the per-person-selected hybrid is at {{cm:final/v1/conformal_mondrian|d}} and {{cm:final/v2/conformal_mondrian|d}}. The same conformal step on the v1 chain reads {{cm:chain_v1/v1/conformal_mondrian:acc|pct}} at v1's coverage and {{cm:chain_v1/v2/conformal_mondrian:acc|pct}} at v2's, and at alpha = 0.10 it answers {{cf:chain_v1/0.1:coverage|pct}} of windows at {{cf:chain_v1/0.1:acc|pct}} and alerts {{cf:chain_v1/0.1:alert_share_all|pct}} of hypoxic windows, against {{cf:deployed_R/0.1:coverage|pct}}, {{cf:deployed_R/0.1:acc|pct}} and {{cf:deployed_R/0.1:alert_share_all|pct}} for the deployed hybrid: **the chain-only control, which the app can run behind `?engine=logistic`, has the higher point estimates and answers more windows**; the intervals overlap. The loss therefore comes from the hybrid score, not from the conformal step. At alpha = 0.10 the deployed pipeline calls {{cf:deployed_R/0.1:confident_miss|pct}} of hypoxic windows Normal (target 10%). Set coverage holds approximately pooled and fails per person: person 1 has {{cpp:deployed_R/0.1/hof_100001:confident_miss|pct}} of its hypoxic windows called Normal. The thresholds shipped in the app (`app/data/conformal.json`) are fit on the out-of-fold scores of all six people for this pipeline and are therefore in-sample on the replay demo.

